Z||000008||BBBAD GT||10-08-2001||09:58 PM||||  <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by falconhulk:<BR><B>Wrong the fastest is the Cobra.  The truck has more horsepower(380 to 344) but is heavier.  </B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>The cobra is only rated at 320 bhp, and its finally all there for 2001 (they were missing some in 1999...but they fixed that).  The Fastest Ford is the Cobra R, about as fast as the ZO6 Vette.<P><A HREF="http://home.att.net/~nomercy5.0/" TARGET=_blank>My Street Stang</A><BR>11.13 @ 127 <P><p>[This message has been edited by BBBAD GT (edited 10-08-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000009||BlackStang95||10-09-2001||12:17 AM||||Hey people, I'm spektrums friend that he raced and I just wanted to add to his story.  My engine is totally stock...150 hp at 4000 rpms.  (It's a little known fact the 95's had a 5 hp boost.) I have a K+N, but so does he, and his is brand new, as well as performance plugs and wires, while mine are older stock ones. 215 lbs of tq compared to his 160. My engine is far from new, it has 70k miles on it, his has 96k. My rear differential is also broken and whines. When we raced I had him off the line by a couple of feet, then he caught up and pulled ahead by a foot or so, and we were dead even like that till about 80 when a car pulled out and we stopped.  Morale of the story, the slowest Mustangs can run with the fastest fieros  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  I'm not saying Fieros arent cool, they're nice, I really like his car and I can't wait to see what it can do after his restoration/engine swap. I just wanted to get my opinion out because everyone who doesnt drive one hates on Mustangs, I mean i know we're the best but damn.  Import ricers, crapmaros/firechickens, monte carlos, corvettes that actually race, bmw, volkswagon people, and now fiero people all talk about Mustang kills.  They need to just admit theyre a great car, theres plenty of fags that drive em, and some women, but what do you expect when they sell 200k a year (thats about what the fiero sold in its lifetime) by law of averages alone youre gonna get your idiots.  Bottom line, dont hate on fellow detroit muscle, its the ricers we need to **** up.  Nothin but love to yall.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000010||Slammed Fiero||10-09-2001||12:43 AM||||Ok.... First off We have a 95 5.0ltr. It's slow. Grated a Cobra R is fast...this is not. My fiero (v6 4spd) will eat it, As will our LT1 Caprice wagon. I got smoked a few weeks ago my a lincoln Mark 8 in the mustang. He pulled on me from about 70mph up.<P>Fiero's sold Closer to 1/2 a million (460,xxx) , pretty good for a 2 seater. It beat the vette in sales every year it was produced and smoked the mr2 in sales in a total of Mk1 and Mk2 production. Not bad for a niche market car , even with bad press, plus the economy wasn't in great shape during the 80s' ...but we won't get into that.<P><BR>6cyl mustang weighs 3100 LBs. Most GT fast backs are some 400lbs lighter if not more. I don't know the point in mentioning this , but it's true.<P>As for the slowest mustang hanging witht he Fastest Fiero..ahhh Perhaps fastest showroom Fiero. But there's a member here named 1FST2M6..a legendary fellow that has 2.8ltrs thats a pretty basic motor with a mild rebuild I believe that has put down some passes that would humble even the mighty Cobra R. (he runs NOS). Incase you didn't know , Fiero's are Notorius For engine swaps<P><BR>I won't even get into handling. The 2 cars are hard to compare. Personally I would be kinda pissed if a 2.8 Fiero that is 14+ years old hung with my 6 year old 3.8ltr mustang. Not to be mean , but excuses are just that....excuses.<P>It's apples and oranges really. <P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/mycar_1.JPG"> <P>------------------<BR>Jonathan McCreery<BR>86 GT 4spd<BR>Koni's , Coilovers, Big Bars , 17" Trmotorsports Typhoons , 11.25" vented discs, Wilwood 4 Piston Calipers , Pirelli P Zero's, Short Shift, No cat , Cold air induction , Geni Stainless tips, White face gauges , Momo shift , momo pedals, Big Bore TB, 70Hp Shot of NOS Autocrossed , Tracked , Dragged? (soon) abused.||||reg||1
Z||000011||BlackStang95||10-09-2001||12:54 AM||||I know exactly what my car weighs...and what fieros way...dont know why you brought that up. It makes sense a car a foot and a half longer and with a real body and a bigger engine would weigh more.  I dont feel bad at all his 14 year old car hung with my 6 year old car...for many reasons, one is I know the only reason they are remotely fast is the great getrag tranxaxle that has some high gearing...3.84 i think my friend told me.  My car has broken 2.53's.   The other reason is his car cost more in 87 than mine did in 94.  adjusting for inflation thats quite a gap.  5.0 mustangs are not slow, they are legendary for performance, I'll take any in good shape and kill any stock showroom fiero you bring.  Yes I knew fieros were notorious for engine swaps, and there are many great ones.  You can make any car fast.  It's not apples and oranges, its red appleas and green apples.||||reg||5
Z||000012||BlackStang95||10-09-2001||01:04 AM||||Some more..the fieros didnt sell 460,xxx, they sold 370,167.  A long way from 500k. And youd do well not to get into handling...the cobra r pulls 0.99g on the skidpad, not to mention having power steering.||||reg||1
Z||000013||Slammed Fiero||10-09-2001||01:15 AM||||Ok , your getting ahead of yourself here.<P>Real body. Fiero's are built like Tanks. I can tell you from racing them for the last 5 years , they have a very real , overbuilt frame. This more than compensates for the lack of a metal body.<P>Getrags do not have a 3.84 Ratio. The fastest Tranny in a Fiero is a 3.65 Muncie 4spd , available in 85 and early 86.<P>Your motor is bigger granted..But it has aluminum heads..Fiero motor is all iron ..a boat anchor.<P>If your car is a 6cyl 95 Mustang it has the same weiner ass 2.73 Gears my 95 5.0ltr has.<BR>(This is from a Ford Dealer Spec book , my uncle has a SVT dealership I get lotsa cool info) <A HREF="http://www.kennedyford.ca" TARGET=_blank>www.kennedyford.ca</A> <P>Your engine weighs 351Lbs according to Ford<BR>A Fiero motor Weighs 350lbs. So your right , your motor does weigh more    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>Ok once again to point out. I have a 95 5.0ltr 30 feet away , several members here can attest to the ownership. And a stock V6 Fiero running a getrag 5spd , or a 4spd would be just as fast or faster.<P>Legendary for performance yes. But in reality..not all that fast stock. What makes it legendary is the following and aftermarket it has.<P><BR>It is apples and organges.<P>Fiero 2 seat full independant suspension 4 wheel disc mid engine car.<P>mustang , front engine , rear drive , solid rear axle car.<P>2 Different cars , 2 Different Markets , end of story<P><BR>And as for the handling..you failed to mention the Cobra R has Independent suspension.... Your car and 97% of the other 5.0ltrs on the road don't. I don't have to talk about handling , anyone who knows me has a good idea about handling. <P>you wanna play magazine Tag... 84 Corvette z51 Broke 1 G on crap ass Goodyear GSC's off the showroom floor.<P> Ahh What does power steerign have to do with handling?<P>JM <P><BR>[This message has been edited by Slammed Fiero (edited 10-09-2001).]<p>[This message has been edited by Slammed Fiero (edited 10-09-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000014||BlackStang95||10-09-2001||01:24 AM||||Sigh...here we go again<P>I know they have a solid body, I know they were very safe cars, I was saying the plastic contributes to light weight.  DUH<BR>retard.<P>2.73 is still a lot worse than 3.65 <P>And I dont know what else to say, If my 3.8L could run with and very possibilty beat a v6 fiero what would it do with 65 more horses and 80 more lbs of torque?  Beat it clean.  Enough said.<P>Not to mention 94 and 95 were the slowest years for Mustangs.  Maybe we should be comparing them to an 84 SE.  The newer Gt's can run high 13's off the showroom floor, which is what a lot of your v8 modified fieros seem to be running.  <P>"Fiero 2 seat full independant suspension 4 wheel disc mid engine car.<P>mustang , front engine , rear drive , solid rear axle car."<P>you dont make much sense.  Mustangs have 4 wheel disc, some have fully independent suspension.  Mid engine yes...but if you make that a class youre gonna ahve a very small number of cars.  Don't nitpick, in general they are simaler.  I never meant to start a debate like this but if you want you can BRING IT, WHAT?! IM RIGHT HERE, IM NOT GOING ANYWHERE.  sorry, been listening to dmx's new album. Peace.<P>||||reg||4
Z||000015||Slammed Fiero||10-09-2001||01:33 AM||||Your post shows the degree of your intelligence. I shot down all your points..<P>You call me a retard? ??<P>2.73 is worse thana 3.65 granted... But look at your torque curve!!!<P>The plastic doesn't contribute all that much in retrospect. Mustangs are commonly known for neededing Sub frame connectors. Fiero's  , due to their tank like attributes don't need such things when power is increased , I'm sure V8 archie can attest to this. So you see you have to look at things more 2 Dimensionally than spitting up the #'s<P>Another case...and we see this a lot here at pennocks..of some guy feeling bad about his car , whatever it may be ..because it got beat by a Fiero..a Car people love to hate.<P>Uneducated Neanderthals.  ||||reg||1
