Z||000030||Groove Champion||10-09-2001||08:01 PM||||I haven't been here long enough to introduce myself. This is my second post. I live North of Oakville Ontario and use to work for ford. I have plenty of seat time in Mustangs on the track and street. I have also had the pleasure of owning a few. As well now I have a 87 GT Fiero.<P>The Fiero is a more sporting car to drive. Skid pad #'s mean little unless you drive in 300ft circles. The Fiero , while not as fast as a mustang in a straight line , would no doubt beat iton a track<P>I used to run the players series in a showroom setup 92 5.0ltr. I can tell you that my fiero with a set of Toyo RA1's is a better balanced more confident car. PERIOD.<P>Anyone can go fast in a straight line. I know guys with OMni 2.2 turbo's running mid 12's on the street.<P>And just on a Side note.. If Slammed Fiero's Dad is Paul McCreery which I think it is. Your arguing with the son of a very well know racer  , and from what I have heard around Canadian Autosports Jon is making quite a name for himself on and off the track.<P>I'm sure there must be some mustang forum where you can discuss your car.<P>GC.<P><BR>||||reg||1
Z||000031||banditbalz||10-09-2001||09:16 PM||||Welcome to the forum, Groove! Always nice to chat with a local Fiero owner. As a friend of SlammedFiero, I can attest that Paul McCreery is in fact his legendary father. Had the chance to meet him at last years Michigan show.<P>Here's a pic of a '95 5.0 auto that just couldn't quit keep up with my GT. It belongs to a friend of mine, Sascha, has true SVT side ehaust and all the usual bolt ons. Beautiful car, love cruising in it, but it is not a fast car. I embarrassed him at 3 seperate sets of red lights. I had a trunk full of groceries, my girlfriend, my dog and a hot pizza on my lap. Even at 15.2, I don't consider my GT a "fast car". It's only a 4 speed, stock V6 with a K+N air filter!<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/SaschaGeo.jpg"> <BR><P>------------------<BR>Silver 86 GT<BR>completely stock,<BR>completely fast!||||reg||1
Z||000032||Spektrum-87GT||10-09-2001||10:04 PM||||guy, calm down, i said enough alright? look, your dad might be a top notch racer, and thats great, but you're not going to sit here and tell me a 5.0 95 mustang is slower than a stock fiero gt in a drag, or the 3.8 gets killed by a stock fiero gt. I'll trust the pro drivers statistics and not some kids experience racing against them. On the track, a fiero gt will beat the mustang hands down, but in a dead straight away drag, a mustang gt will dust the fiero gt, because lets face it, the fiero gt in stock for is SLOW, a toyota camry and nissan altima can beat it in a race, end of story. I'm talking about cars with manual transmissions here, because most stock automatics will kill performance. Another thing, just because your dad is rich and you had an oppurtunity to race does not qualify you as as an expert on car performance. If you did your research, you would find that a degree in automotive technology CAN qualify you as a car performance expert, but you're a little too ignorant to see that. I'm sorry for the flame, I tried to resist, but one thing I cannot stand is a rich kid that thinks he knows everything about cars and in reality he knows very little. I never claimed to know a lot, but blackstang95 has been going to school for car performance(not marketing) so he DOES know. He never said his car would beat it on the track, shoot, he just said it would run with a fiero gt in a straight away, and IT WILL, I can tell you this from first hand experience, and i can drive a manual better than the next guy, so don't tell me i'm a bad driver. End of story, and unless I made a mistake somewhere, I dont want to hear anything else about it.<P> <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Slammed Fiero:<BR><B>Just to clear things up....<BR> <BR>Again We have a 5.0ltr mustang...last I checked not GM<BR>A nissan pathfinder...not GM again<BR>1994 911 RS Porsche<BR>72 911 S porsche<P>and a slew of other cars not built by the General.<P>The new explorer has independent suspension..better than your mustang infact. All the magazines have raved about the increase in ride quality.<P>JM </B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>||||reg||1
Z||000033||grinthock||10-09-2001||10:22 PM||||I have seen banditbalz and he has seen me BOTH beat 5.0 Mustangs to the 60FT on many many ocassions, and at the end of the 1/4 they ain't that far ahead.<P>In the city in my 4-spd mostly stock fiero (and banditbalz as well) we RIP mustangs at lights.  Ok, you wanna do the 1/4 or more mile?  YEah they are gonna be ahead!   There ain't no replacement for displacement at that point.<P>BUT I do'nt have enough brains to join this arguement, so have fun guys, I am back to listening now.||||reg||1
Z||000034||FieroKyle||10-09-2001||10:39 PM||||Alright, this guy starting to piss me off. I have sat here too long and now I can't stand it. <BR>Point #1: The Fiero GT and Mustang 5.0 are quick cars, not fastest, but by far not slow pokes. Both running low 15's on a quarter for stock cars isn't shabby.<BR>Point #2: The 5.0 lacks because of its terrible gearing, has potential, but it slower than ****  for a "high performance" V-8 for a so called muscle car.<BR>Point #3: I raced my friend who has a 95' GT not too long ago (2 weeks). Pretty stock. He has a K&N, I have no cat converter. I have an 85 GT.  <A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum6/HTML/003580.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum6/HTML/003580.html</A>  <BR>Please see this post for the explanation of race.<BR>The only point where is 5.0 really showed my Fiero that I couldn't keep up with him on the express as well is with his top gear. He had the 5-speed manual in it, and did it haul after about 120 mph.<BR>Point #4: We are comparing a mid-engined V-6 sportscar from the mid 80's to a mid 90's 5.0 V-8 in a Mustang. That to me is apples and oranges. Thats one whole decade in a technology gap. May be a Camaro vs. Mustang, or Mr2 vs. Fiero is fair, but not your points.<BR>Point #5: V-6 Mustangs suck ass and are slower than hell, nuff said. If it isn't a 5.0, it won't beat a Fiero if both are stock. <BR>Point #6: My car being 10 years older than this kid's mustang GT I raced, and come within 3/4 of a car length on him in a quarter mile is very impressive to me, and trust me, all the people gloating "hes got a v-8, why race? he gonna waste you so bad" their jaws dropped when I kepted up with this Mudstain. I even had him by a half of a car length at the 1/8 on my second run. So all the guys saying they beat a 5.0 in their Fiero, even though the guy driving the 5.0 probably didn't know what he was doing, he has pretty much every advantage all the way around.<P>If you would like to continue your little argument, go ahead, me and my friends have the facts and expirience while you continue to talk out your ass.<P>Kyle - 85' GT<BR>||||reg||4
Z||000035||FieroKyle||10-09-2001||10:48 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Spektrum-87GT:<BR><B>guy, calm down, i said enough alright? look, your dad might be a top notch racer, and thats great, but you're not going to sit here and tell me a 5.0 95 mustang is slower than a stock fiero gt in a drag, or the 3.8 gets killed by a stock fiero gt. I'll trust the pro drivers statistics and not some kids experience racing against them. On the track, a fiero gt will beat the mustang hands down, but in a dead straight away drag, a mustang gt will dust the fiero gt, because lets face it, the fiero gt in stock for is SLOW, a toyota camry and nissan altima can beat it in a race, end of story. I'm talking about cars with manual transmissions here, because most stock automatics will kill performance. Another thing, just because your dad is rich and you had an oppurtunity to race does not qualify you as as an expert on car performance. If you did your research, you would find that a degree in automotive technology CAN qualify you as a car performance expert, but you're a little too ignorant to see that. I'm sorry for the flame, I tried to resist, but one thing I cannot stand is a rich kid that thinks he knows everything about cars and in reality he knows very little. I never claimed to know a lot, but blackstang95 has been going to school for car performance(not marketing) so he DOES know. He never said his car would beat it on the track, shoot, he just said it would run with a fiero gt in a straight away, and IT WILL, I can tell you this from first hand experience, and i can drive a manual better than the next guy, so don't tell me i'm a bad driver. End of story, and unless I made a mistake somewhere, I dont want to hear anything else about it.<P> </B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>You really piss me off with that comment. What makes him a rich kid just because his dad races?? There are many people that put every dime they make into racing and they are not the richest people in the world. They keep adjusting their race cars, putting money into it slowly but surely. Then they get some expierence, win some races, get a few more bucks from may be a sponsor or a win in a race. Get the car better and keep it outta of the wall and bam, your doing pretty good in the racing world. May not be making a living off it, but your getting to the point where its getting the potential. The rich kids are the ones that get a brand new race car, but since they just want to race, usually don't have the knowledge and lack in races losing almost every fricken time.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000036||FieroKyle||10-09-2001||10:54 PM||||And another thing (I keep thinking of more stuff as I vent off here  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">) when does social class ever a issue here. There are people who love a Fiero just as much as the other guy here and one has a 84' SE that runs sometimes, then theres the guy that has a show car with all the stuff in it. We respect everybody here except for people who just flair off on something thats not true and just talk to hear themselves (I guess you can make fun of me here and call me hypocritical since this is my 3rd straight post  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">). To my point is that since when does income really matter in what kind of car do you drive or what it is. I see people who live in a trailor, but has a fairly new Corvette sitting in the yard, thats just how they want to live, one thing is more important to the other guy.||||reg||1
