Z||000048||Slammed Fiero||10-10-2001||01:25 PM||||Wow ..your a total dumbass.<P>Put better shocks on a mustang and it will handle better than a fiero??<P>No skippy , you have a solid rear axle. The problem goes far deeper than ride height and swapping shocks. A live axle car will not handle as well as a Independently sprung car.<P>you have no knowledge what so ever about how to make a car handle. Keep to your mustang and it's 1960's for falcon suspension. <P>I could get into the logistics about why a mustang will never handle as well as a car with independent suspension , but whats the point? Read a book called "how to make your car handle" and a few others.<P>Th only vette your 6cyl mustang will beat is a 53 BLue flame 6. <P>I think a lot of people have written you off as a total dumbass..if not they will after a comment like "Duhhh gee wally change the shocks" It shows your degree of intelligence. Suspension modification is an exact science, made up of a lot more than swapping shocks. Sway bars , spring rates, weight jacking , understeer , oversteer, compression, rebound , camber , caster. all sorts of things that you need to read up on to really understand.<P>What grade are you in?? Not to label young people , but your posts scream ..'I'm in Highschool and I'm the fastest" I remember kids like you. Knew everything..just ask them!<P>I hope cliff closes this thread. <P>JM <p>[This message has been edited by Slammed Fiero (edited 10-10-2001).]||||reg||1
